; Example 6: MXFP4 block quantization (OCP Microscaling)
; Divides vector into 32-element blocks, shares 8-bit exponent per block.
; Lower compute cost than Lloyd-Max + QJL, slightly lower quality.
; Good for: latency-sensitive scenarios where quality loss is acceptable.
LDV V0, [0x00000000]
GVNS V0, 0
GVNS V0, 1
GVNS V0, 2
POLAR V0
MXPACK V0, MXFP4
STV V0, [0x10000000]
HALT
